  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>R</mi></math> is a function such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>∀</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;<br />\rthen the period of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8757;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Replacing&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi></math> by <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> in <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, we get,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> &hellip; <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />On subtracting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Now,&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>"
  }
